; examples/maps-sets.nx — collection literals.
;
; nexis now supports maps {} and sets #{} as runtime values.
; Both quoted compound literals and runtime-computed forms work.
; Keys/values/elements can be arbitrary expressions; duplicates
; collapse per Clojure semantics (later-wins for maps, set-
; semantics for sets).
;
; The runtime backing is the CHAMP persistent map/set
; with structural sharing. Hash + equality come from the
; dispatch layer (same machinery used everywhere else).

(let [project-id :nexis
      version    :v0-2-alpha
      tags       #{:phase-3 :collections :ready}]
  {:project project-id
   :version version
   :tags    tags
   :status  :shipped})
